#
# Response headers for the `starboard` Worker's static assets (served from
# the deployed site root; the format Pages also uses).
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE, adapted from coding-standards' website. `pnpm build`
# runs scripts/csp-postbuild.mjs after `astro build`, which replaces the two
# placeholders on every Content-Security-Policy line in dist/_headers:
#   __CSP_SCRIPT_HASHES__  SHA-256 hashes of every inline <script> Starlight
#                          emits (theme provider, sidebar state, search shortcut)
#   __CSP_STYLE_HASHES__   SHA-256 hashes of any inline <style> (normally none;
#                          astro.config sets build.inlineStylesheets: 'never')
# so script-src and style-src never need 'unsafe-inline'. Inline style
# attributes are allowed per page by a <meta> CSP the post-build step adds
# (style-src-attr 'unsafe-hashes' <that page's hashes>); browsers enforce
# both policies, so only those exact attributes pass.
#
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' on /* is required by Pagefind (the docs' search), which
# compiles a WebAssembly module; it does not permit JavaScript eval().
#
# /app/* is the PWA (web/app). Pages Cloudflare matches with both rules get
# both Content-Security-Policy values, joined into one header: two policies,
# and the browser enforces each. The /app/* line is the site's policy plus
# what the PWA needs, 'wasm-unsafe-eval' for its WebAssembly core and
# worker-src 'self' for the core's and the app map's workers, so it is the
# same whether Cloudflare sends one policy or both. The PWA's own index.html
# also carries its build's CSP (web/app/vite.config.ts) as a meta tag.
#
# Cloudflare Web Analytics: Cloudflare adds its beacon to the site's pages
# at the edge (it is not in the build), so /* allows that one script,
# https://static.cloudflareinsights.com, and the reports it sends to
# https://cloudflareinsights.com. It is cookieless and counts visits. The
# app is kept out of it: an /app/ page's address carries the user's project
# (#/map/<screen id>), and the app promises nothing leaves the device. So
# /app/* sends Cache-Control: no-transform, which tells Cloudflare not to
# add the beacon, and the /app/* policy, which the browser enforces as well
# as /*'s, still allows no third-party script or connection.
#
# Nowhere else is the policy relaxed.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com 'sha256-7eCV4jtsr4t4knb3c4FCRPeu7GGZeOUGE3XvWix0XOQ=' 'sha256-CucRf0bf0xYD/oKdMuRRn1yhi9AJeUlkP4LSbkp47Ls=' 'sha256-f/zAUE74ucc3JYp4r4QQvkJofoQdkOIhHYK+jeZ6eko=' 'sha256-wX2yOADeV+NMngflD5uYi3vl50SHC4sfM1EmylVjlX4=' 'sha256-yiTapURQAzVYqJIJXL03Gepg/022hHZUVvS4f8isCN8='; style-src 'self'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'

/app/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, no-transform
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' 'sha256-7eCV4jtsr4t4knb3c4FCRPeu7GGZeOUGE3XvWix0XOQ=' 'sha256-CucRf0bf0xYD/oKdMuRRn1yhi9AJeUlkP4LSbkp47Ls=' 'sha256-f/zAUE74ucc3JYp4r4QQvkJofoQdkOIhHYK+jeZ6eko=' 'sha256-wX2yOADeV+NMngflD5uYi3vl50SHC4sfM1EmylVjlX4=' 'sha256-yiTapURQAzVYqJIJXL03Gepg/022hHZUVvS4f8isCN8='; style-src 'self'; style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'

/*.wasm
  Content-Type: application/wasm
